codex
The family arithmetic itself is sound, but the surrounding “full panel” claim is weaker than it sounds: the database stores only a number, not which reviewers were required. I’m testing whether unrelated seats—including the builder—can substitute for the configured panel while still satisfying both guards. That distinction matters to the owner’s “full set, always” decision.
